========== 第7章: MTA は1台に1つ（sendmail も同じ宣言）。exim4 も sendmail 互換のコマンドを持つ ==========

$ apt-cache show --no-all-versions sendmail-bin | grep -E '^(Provides|Conflicts):'
Provides: mail-transport-agent
Conflicts: mail-transport-agent

$ apt-cache show --no-all-versions exim4 | grep -E '^Depends:'
Depends: debconf (>= 1.4.69) | cdebconf (>= 0.39), exim4-base (<< 4.97-4ubuntu4.8.1), exim4-base (>= 4.97-4ubuntu4.8), exim4-daemon-light (>= 4.97-4ubuntu4.8) | exim4-daemon-heavy (>= 4.97-4ubuntu4.8) | exim4-daemon-custom (>= 4.97-4ubuntu4.8), debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0

$ cd /tmp && apt-get download exim4-base exim4-daemon-light > /dev/null 2>&1; ls /tmp/exim4*.deb; cd /root
/tmp/exim4-base_4.97-4ubuntu4.8_amd64.deb
/tmp/exim4-daemon-light_4.97-4ubuntu4.8_amd64.deb

$ for d in /tmp/exim4*.deb; do dpkg-deb -c $d | grep -E 'sbin/sendmail|bin/mailq|bin/newaliases'; done
lrwxrwxrwx root/root         0 2026-09-23 03:24 ./usr/bin/mailq -> ../sbin/exim4
lrwxrwxrwx root/root         0 2026-09-23 03:24 ./usr/bin/newaliases -> ../sbin/exim4
lrwxrwxrwx root/root         0 2026-09-23 03:24 ./usr/sbin/sendmail -> exim4


========== 第7章: /etc/aliases の右側はカンマで複数（全員に1通ずつ届く） ==========

$ man 5 aliases 2>/dev/null | grep -B2 -A1 'name: value1, value2'
       •      An alias definition has the form

                   name: value1, value2, ...


$ echo 'support: alice, bob' >> /etc/aliases

$ newaliases

$ echo "全員に届くか" | mail -s "カンマで2人" support

$ grep -c "全員に届くか" /var/mail/alice /var/mail/bob
/var/mail/alice:1
/var/mail/bob:1

$ journalctl -t postfix/local --no-pager | tail -2
Oct 13 19:42:42 linuc postfix/local[682]: DC0441185008: to=<alice@lab.local>, orig_to=<support>, relay=local, delay=0.02, delays=0.01/0/0/0, dsn=2.0.0, status=sent (delivered to mailbox)
Oct 13 19:42:42 linuc postfix/local[682]: DC0441185008: to=<bob@lab.local>, orig_to=<support>, relay=local, delay=0.02, delays=0.01/0/0/0.01, dsn=2.0.0, status=sent (delivered to mailbox)


========== 第7章: ~/.forward は1行に1宛先。手元にも残すなら \自分の名前 ==========

$ printf '\\bob\nroot\n' > /home/bob/.forward

$ chown bob:bob /home/bob/.forward; chmod 644 /home/bob/.forward

$ cat /home/bob/.forward
\bob
root

$ echo "手元にも残す" | mail -s "backslash" bob

$ grep -c "手元にも残す" /var/mail/bob /var/mail/root
/var/mail/bob:1
/var/mail/root:1

$ printf 'bob\nroot\n' > /home/bob/.forward

$ echo "バックスラッシュなし" | mail -s "no-backslash" bob

$ grep -c "バックスラッシュなし" /var/mail/bob /var/mail/root
/var/mail/bob:1
/var/mail/root:1

$ printf 'root, lab\n' > /home/bob/.forward

$ echo "1行にカンマで2つ" | mail -s "comma-forward" bob

$ grep -c "1行にカンマで2つ" /var/mail/bob /var/mail/root /var/mail/lab
/var/mail/bob:0
/var/mail/root:1
/var/mail/lab:1

$ man 8postfix local 2>/dev/null | grep -B3 -A4 'own ~/.forward'
       ward file has the same syntax as the right-hand part of an alias.

       When  an  address is found in its own alias expansion, delivery is made
       to the user instead. When a user is listed in the user's own ~/.forward
       file, delivery is made to the user's mailbox instead.  An empty ~/.for‐
       ward file means do not forward mail.

       In order to prevent the mail system from using up unreasonable  amounts


